<td></td><td></td><td align="left">D(42*)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left"><bold>1321</bold></td><td align="left">L</td><td align="left">-</td><td align="left">-</td><td align="left">-</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td align="left">+</td><td align="left">+</td><td align="left">+</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td align="left">D(42*)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left"><bold>1306</bold></td><td align="left">L</td><td align="left">-</td><td align="left">-</td><td align="left">-</td><td align="left">-</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td align="left">+</td><td align="left">+</td><td align="left">-</td><td align="left">-</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td align="left">D(77*)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left"><bold>1317</bold></td><td align="left">L</td><td align="left">-</td><td align="left">-</td><td align="left">-</td><td align="left">nd</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td align="left">+</td><td align="left">+</td><td align="left">+</td><td align="left">+</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td align="left">D(84) hw-G</td><td align="left">1 N</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p><bold><italic>Key</italic></bold>: <sup>1</sup>Sp. = Species; L = lamb; K = kid; <sup>2</sup>Age range per level: <bold>1 </bold>(0 &#x02013; 10 days), <bold>2 </bold>(11&#x02013;21 days), <bold>3 </bold>(22 &#x02013; 49 days), <bold>4 </bold>(50 &#x02013; 77 days), <bold>5 </bold>(78 &#x02013; 98 days), <bold>6 </bold>(99 &#x02013; 126), <bold>7 </bold>(127 &#x02013; 162); <sup>3</sup>D = died (numbers in parentheses indicate day of death); <sup>4</sup>hw-G heartwater confirmed by Giemsa; hw-PCR: heartwater confirmed by pCS20 PCR;</p><p><sup>5</sup><italic>AV: A. variegatum </italic>tick counts on selected study animals; N = nymph; A = adult; *mortality due to coccidial and/or clostridial enteritis; <sup>6</sup>Animal numbers in bold are cases of mortality</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T3"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>